## Box plots that render one point per patient are per-patient derivatives in
## graphical form, so they are withheld with the rest of that material; the
## aggregate attenuation curve is not.
/applied_study_oncology/New_Data/analysis/treatment_exposure_distribution.png
/applied_study_oncology/New_Data/analysis/exposure_rate_distribution.png
/applied_study_oncology/New_Data/analysis/endpoint_distribution_by_treatment.png

## Analysis-output subdirectories of ANY data drop.
##
## The rules above were a denylist keyed to exact directory names, which could
## not survive the addition of a new versioned data directory: New_Data_v2/
## therefore leaked a patient-level endpoint file until commit 41a6c44 was
## rewritten to remove it. These recursive patterns cover every present and
## future analysis/ subtree under applied_study_oncology/, whatever the data
## drop is called, so nothing written by run_domain_diagnostics.R is ever
## tracked again.
/applied_study_oncology/**/analysis/*.csv
/applied_study_oncology/**/analysis/*.rds
/applied_study_oncology/**/analysis/*.log
/applied_study_oncology/**/analysis/*.png
/applied_study_oncology/**/analysis/*.pdf
/applied_study_oncology/geweke_investigation/*.rds
/applied_study_oncology/geweke_investigation/*.md

/applied_study_oncology/Legal_Stuff/
